  "synthesis": "The common thread is open, computationally accessible tooling that organizes bacterial genomes into standardized groups. Robust Cluster Typing applies a Snakemake/Python workflow that uses ribosomal proteins to assign genomes to species-level clusters, demonstrated on Campylobacter. SNP2Cluster-Py provides an open-source Python framework for context-aware core SNP clustering of pathogen isolates, tested on Klebsiella and pneumococcal whole-genome datasets. P2CS-Web is a different kind of contribution: an updated curated resource linking prokaryotic two-component system repertoires to domain architectures, genomic neighbourhoods and sequence clusters. The two preprints present analysis workflows, whereas P2CS-Web is a database update. What is new is the pathogen-agnostic, reproducible treatment of species designation and transmission-cluster analysis from whole-genome data, with ribosomal proteins as the basis for species assignment in the first item.",
